{
  "storeDesc": {
    "message": "Use this reverse image search Chrome extension to trace a photo to its source, identify a product from a screenshot, or compare visual matches. Preview a crop in the Chrome side panel and send it to the providers you choose.\n\n10 search engines, 4 enabled by default\n✅ Google Lens, Bing Visual Search, Yandex Images, and TinEye are enabled and selected on a fresh install.\n✅ Open Settings and choose Add engines to enable any of the six optional providers for your first search.\n✅ Try Baidu or Sogou to search a different index, or use SauceNAO to trace an illustration to its source.\n✅ Try Pinterest for ideas and check SHEIN and Wildberries for products that look like an item in a photo.\n✅ Turn search engines on or off and reorder them in Settings. Your preferences carry over after updating.\n✅ Choose one, several, or all enabled engines. Each opens results in its own tab so you can compare them.\n\nSearch by picture with a right-click\n⚡ Right-click an image on a web page and select an engine from the extension menu to search it.\n⚡ Choose All search engines to run the same lookup with all enabled providers from the submenu.\n⚡ Choose Open image to inspect the picture by itself in a separate tab before running a lookup.\n⚡ On a fresh install, the extension looks for nearby images and sizes of the photo you clicked.\n\nScreenshot image search\n✂️ Click the extension icon in the toolbar to open the Chrome side panel next to the current page.\n✂️ Choose Capture area and draw a rectangle around the part of the visible page you want to check.\n✂️ Leave out captions, menus, and clutter to keep the crop focused on the item you want to search.\n✂️ Select Use capture, check the crop preview, and click Search image after choosing your engines.\n✂️ If Capture area is missing, paste or upload a screenshot you took and search it from the panel.\n\nSearch by photo, clipboard, or URL\n⬆️ Click Choose file to add a saved image or screenshot. Check the preview and pick the providers you want to use.\n⬆️ Drag and drop up to three files in the side panel. Click the thumbnails to review them before you run a search.\n⬆️ Paste a copied image or direct link from your clipboard. The Paste button may ask for access to your clipboard.\n⬆️ Enter a direct HTTP or HTTPS address in Image link, then select Preview link to confirm it’s the right picture.\n⬆️ If the link preview fails to load, you can still search by URL with a provider that supports this type of link.\n⬆️ If an engine is marked Upload only, save the image and click Choose file to run a check with the same provider.\n\nWhat to look for in the results\n⭐ Find the source of an image by checking page dates, captions, and credits on pages that show the same photo.\n⭐ Follow the credit back to a publisher or creator and check how they describe, date, and present the picture.\n⭐ Find a higher-resolution image by comparing the dimensions of copies on several matching pages and listings.\n⭐ Find similar images and note whether the matches show the same subject, an alternate crop, or a second view.\n⭐ Try a second provider if the first set of results shows too few matches or misses details that interest you.\n⭐ Use product search by image to match an item from a saved photo, a listing picture, or a cropped screenshot.\n⭐ Compare a product’s shape and pattern across vendors to tell a close match from the exact item you’re after.\n⭐ See where an image was reused. Compare dates and captions to check how each publisher presented the picture.\n\nWhat gets sent to providers\nℹ️ Your chosen providers receive the image or its URL when you run a search, depending on the input.\nℹ️ The extension may temporarily store the file in your browser while preparing it for the provider.\nℹ️ Previewing a direct image link can contact the site that serves it before you launch your search.\nℹ️ Each provider handles your input under its own rules. Check the preview before you send the file.\n\nGet started in Chrome\n▶️ Select Add to Chrome and open the Extensions menu to pin this extension to your toolbar.\n▶️ Open the side panel and drop in a saved image to try this extension with your own photo.\n▶️ Pick two providers and compare the results in the tabs that open from your first search."
  },
